    {
      "id": "be-s12m-monopolistic-competition-c1",
      "heading": "Environment and limited market power",
      "explanation_md": "**Monopolistic competition** has:\n\n- **Numerous buyers and sellers**\n- **Differentiated products**: each firm faces a **downward sloping demand curve**, but consumers see the products as **close substitutes**.\n- **Free entry and exit**: **zero profits in the long run**.\n\nLike a monopoly, the firm can **price above MC** and its sales depend on its price, and its MR behaves like a monopolist's. But **other brands make its demand more elastic**, and free entry hurts profits, so it has **limited market power**.",
      "example_ids": [],
      "key_terms": [],
      "exam_line": "Many firms, differentiated products, free entry: downward sloping demand but limited market power.",
      "clarification": null,
