    {
      "id": "be-s12m-monopolistic-competition-c2",
      "heading": "Short run and long run",
      "explanation_md": "**Short run:** maximize profits **like a monopolist**: produce where **MR = MC** and charge the price on the demand curve. The firm can earn a **profit**.\n\n**Long run:** with free entry, other firms enter and their **new brands steal market share**, shifting your demand down **until profits are zero**: **P = AC**.",
      "example_ids": [],
      "key_terms": [],
      "exam_line": "Short run: MR = MC, possible profit. Long run: entry shifts demand down until P = AC and profit is zero.",
      "clarification": null,
      "check_questions": [
        {
          "id": "be-s12m-monopolistic-competition-q-e4894c0a",
          "type": "mcq",
          "stem": "In long-run equilibrium under monopolistic competition:",
          "options": [
            "P = AC and profit is zero",
            "P = MC and profit is positive",
            "The firm shuts down"
          ],
          "answer": "P = AC and profit is zero",
